<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47454" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tănăis</span></b> , is,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τάναϊς.</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The river Tanais</i>, now <i>the
			Don</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 1, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 2, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 2, 6 al.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 12,
				24, § 78</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 7, 7, § 19</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Hor.
				C. 3, 10, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 29, 28</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 15,
			24</span></i> et saep.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tanaimque nivalem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 4, 517</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Liv. 38, 38</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tănăītae</span></b> ,
				ārum, m., <i>the inhabitants of the country near the Don</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 7,
				7, § 22</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Amm. 31, 3,
			1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tă-năītis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., <i>she that lives by the Don</i>, i. e. <i>an
			Amazon</i>, <i><span class="en">Sen. Hippol. 399</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>A river in Numidia</i>, <i><span class="en">Sall. J.
				90, 2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tă-năītĭcus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to the Don</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">potor Scythicae undae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Carm. 5, 479</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crusta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 11, 96</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A proper name of a man</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A.
				12, 513</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 1, 1, 105</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
